From 6dff53e17a866edb2552906f0cec3fdcc5d5ad4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Upamanyu Sharma <sharma.upamanyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:25:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] wal: truncate a reused N.tmp in the file pipeline

filePipeline.alloc opened 0.tmp/1.tmp without O_TRUNC. A cut interrupted
by a crash after writing its headers into N.tmp leaves them there; the
next incarnation's cut writes its own, possibly shorter, headers over
them, so the stale remnant stays under the records appended after the
cut. A WAL record's CRC covers its Data only, so a power loss that keeps
an appended frame but its one-byte Type leaves the remnant's byte there,
and when it is a state or snapshot type the restart reads an entry as a
hard state or a snapshot record, with a valid CRC.

Open N.tmp with O_TRUNC (createNewWALFile(fpath, true), as Create does
for its first segment): the file is then preallocated from empty, every
byte under a fresh frame is zero, and a torn Type reads as type 0, which
ReadAll reports as an error.

TestFilePipelineTruncatesStaleTmp checks that a reused 0.tmp comes back
all zeros; TestWALTypeTearStaleTmp now asserts that the restart on the
torn image fails or reads only records the WAL wrote. Both fail before
this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
